From: Garu667, the VIctory-NVIDIA contributors, and PortVI contributors
Subject: Allocate distinct console threads for tiled multidimensional compute groups
Upstream: https://github.com/trustno1-coder/VIctory-NVIDIA/pull/30 (2dc3df1c72275a1086330ad3b7cba7f9494fe874)

Reserve thread IDs from a group counter for multi-wave, multidimensional
compute programs that depend on lane order. The counter has its own shared
storage and partial waves reserve from the end of the group. Programs using
all 32 KiB of guest LDS keep the existing path. Translation source changes
already invalidate both disk and in-memory shader caches on this base.

